{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"t":"Test 1","x":0.1296296286983788,"y":0.098837209551669858,"h":0.014534882858869502,"c":1,"w":0.057613169352213556},{"x":0.13168724269547327,"t":"Questions 27-32","y":0.14389534871137621,"w":0.16666666666666663,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.17726737341472776,"c":1,"h":0.016046580212416672,"w":0.34979423522949221,"t":"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","x":0.12962963125167315},{"x":0.12954884469129954,"c":1,"t":"Write the correct letter in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet.","h":0.017890730229929264,"y":0.20808581639790125,"w":0.54339879353841147},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.12962961989734312,"y":0.24263839811058496,"t":"27 The writer refers to visitors to New York to illustrate the point that","w":0.6193415832519531,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.45267491658528647,"y":0.26884570091175342,"t":"exploration is an intrinsic element of being human.","x":0.21399175970437681},{"w":0.41563786824544269,"y":0.28474676064411164,"x":0.20781892600290131,"t":"most people are enthusiastic about exploring.","h":0.016195524146054296,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"C","w":0.016460905075073251,"x":0.17489711936134639,"y":0.3037790695798932,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"x":0.20979849356529237,"y":0.3018888773110906,"t":"exploration can lead to surprising results.","h":0.016594276832607502,"c":1,"w":0.37463938395182295},{"t":"D","h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"y":0.31976744163389981,"x":0.17283950624170605,"w":0.024691357612609877},{"w":0.36213991800944006,"y":0.31831395332989132,"c":1,"h":0.015988372380376759,"t":"most people find exploration daunting.","x":0.19753086395671876},{"t":"28 According to the second paragraph, what is the writer's view of explorers?","x":0.129629632980993,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.69958847045898431,"y":0.3444767440400045,"c":1},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"Their discoveries have brought both benefits and disadvantages.","x":0.21604938762732237,"y":0.37063953475024447,"w":0.57818929036458333},{"t":"B","x":0.17489711937604363,"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"y":0.3880813951222718},{"w":0.016460905075073251,"x":0.17489711935546751,"y":0.40406976719349275,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"C"},{"t":"D","x":0.17489711937604363,"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.42151162768041139,"c":1,"w":0.016460905075073223},{"y":0.388081395213278,"x":0.21604937710685107,"w":0.34156379699707035,"t":"Their main value is in teaching others.","h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1},{"x":0.21810700516767015,"t":"They act on an urge that is common to everyone.","w":0.4382715861002604,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054296,"y":0.40400471131574855},{"x":0.2181070084930796,"y":0.41860465134967473,"h":0.017496644257095073,"w":0.60493825276692703,"t":"They tend to be more attracted to certain professions than to others.","c":1},{"w":0.617283935546875,"y":0.44611307446130311,"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"29 The writer refers to a description of Egdon Heath to suggest that","c":1,"x":0.12962963714601453},{"h":0.019703291049413707,"y":0.46945670663043226,"c":1,"x":0.217987924275659,"t":"Hardy was writing about his own experience of exploration.","w":0.5248936971028646},{"t":"B","w":0.016460905075073223,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.4898255811687835,"x":0.17489711937604363},{"t":"C","y":0.50581395324000444,"w":0.016460905075073251,"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.17489711935546751,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.016460905075073223,"t":"D","x":0.17489711937604363,"y":0.52325581372692298,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.48837209286098782,"w":0.46707819620768232,"x":0.21604937952798972,"h":0.016044868316470673,"c":1,"t":"Hardy was mistaken about the nature of exploration."},{"c":1,"x":0.21597285042467093,"h":0.019291944020768947,"w":0.51250132242838542,"t":"Hardy's aim was to investigate people's emotional states.","y":0.50358437695979807},{"x":0.21604938103725288,"y":0.52179034160051241,"c":1,"w":0.45473251342773435,"h":0.016000356213644928,"t":"Hardy's aim was to show the attraction of isolation."},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"w":0.66049382527669276,"t":"In the fourth paragraph, the writer refers to 'a golden age' to suggest that","c":1,"x":0.16049382820200889,"y":0.54651162773639572},{"x":0.21810700678697723,"c":1,"y":0.57412790684339676,"w":0.65020573933919268,"h":0.014534883982160851,"t":"the amount of useful information produced by exploration has decreased."},{"t":"fewer people are interested in exploring than in the 19th century.","y":0.59010600697825,"w":0.57613169352213545,"c":1,"x":0.21399176645638951,"h":0.015998644317698818},{"y":0.60755813930831837,"w":0.016460905075073223,"x":0.17489711937604363,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"C","c":1},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"recent developments have made exploration less exciting.","y":0.60600706713387742,"c":1,"w":0.52263371785481771,"x":0.21399178855201492},{"x":0.17489711937604363,"t":"D","y":0.62499999977343457,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.016460905075073223},{"w":0.54541203816731776,"h":0.018708877204023255,"c":1,"t":"we are wrong to think that exploration is no longer necessary.","x":0.21598576835232811,"y":0.62270175146235274},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.12962962974214251,"y":0.64970930214856681,"w":0.024691357612609877,"c":1,"t":"31"},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"t":"In the sixth paragraph, when discussing the definition of exploration, the writer","w":0.69547322591145833,"x":0.17283951863211502,"y":0.64958775025259607,"c":1},{"x":0.17449142979832152,"w":0.1076604080200195,"c":1,"h":0.01513221659845676,"t":"argues that","y":0.66734634365185541},{"h":0.017018715821390806,"t":"people tend to relate exploration to their own professional interests.","x":0.218033749025732,"w":0.59888473510742191,"c":1,"y":0.69095483966748084},{"c":1,"y":0.70930232586196984,"t":"B","x":0.17489711937604363,"w":0.016460905075073251,"h":0.013081394460653373},{"y":0.70763150127840124,"c":1,"t":"certain people are likely to misunderstand the nature of exploration.","h":0.017870854713610718,"x":0.21804218868527622,"w":0.60093643188476564},{"x":0.21604938173115404,"h":0.016014052504504606,"w":0.50617284138997398,"t":"the generally accepted definition has changed over time.","y":0.72526501740064819,"c":1},{"x":0.17489711937604363,"t":"D","y":0.74273255791296955,"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"t":"historians and scientists have more valid definitions than the general public.","c":1,"y":0.74116607772302678,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.21604939087791025,"w":0.67489710489908861},{"c":1,"y":0.76744186027393901,"t":"32","x":0.12962962936976552,"w":0.028806584676106778,"h":0.014534883982160851},{"c":1,"x":0.16249208593914288,"t":"In the last paragraph, the writer explains that he is interested in","y":0.76698556285456909,"w":0.5721567789713542,"h":0.018600141482583488},{"w":0.63168726603190106,"h":0.014558851648696858,"c":1,"t":"how someone's personality is reflected in their choice of places to visit.","y":0.79358068336264864,"x":0.21810698418882851},{"y":0.81104651140134154,"t":"B","w":0.016460905075073223,"x":0.17489711937604363,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"t":"C","x":0.17489711959189586,"y":0.82848837190547464,"w":0.018518517812093099,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1},{"y":0.84447674397505423,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"D","w":0.016460905075073223,"x":0.17489711939074087},{"h":0.018318553695409134,"c":1,"t":"the human ability to cast new light on places that may be familiar.","y":0.80919231383175494,"x":0.21801646542357864,"w":0.58040496826171872},{"c":1,"t":"how travel writing has evolved to meet changing demands.","y":0.82695628046432557,"h":0.015860992269886687,"x":0.22010463175572378,"w":0.52273483276367183},{"c":1,"t":"the feelings that writers develop about the places that they explore.","x":0.21604939948127641,"y":0.84302325603206762,"w":0.59876541137695305,"h":0.015988371257085521},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"y":0.91715116260773688,"t":"26","x":0.12962962916420143,"w":0.026748971939086902}]}